IMPORT `spr-part8-credits-general`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173) -- PART 8 (National Insurance Credits), Chapter 3: regulations 29 to 39.
-- Source: plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-04-06 (uksi-2015-173.txt); not the official text.
--
-- Every credit here is for a week, named by its first day, and is out of reach of a week beginning before 6 April 2016 (regulation
-- 24(2), fork F22), so each rule begins with `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week`. Figures and tests of the parent
-- legislation (the lower earnings limit, the qualifying earnings factor, the small profits threshold, whether an election by a
-- married woman is in force, whether a person is "ordinarily resident") are stated inputs. Where the Secretary of State "considers"
-- something, the consideration is an input (a fact about an official's judgment), never presumed.

§ `Part 8, Chapter 3 -- credits for a qualifying year or a post-commencement qualifying year`

§§ `Regulation 39: the time limit for an application`

-- (a): for regulations 34(1)(b), 36 and 37, received before the end of the year following that in which the week falls, or within
-- further time the Secretary of State or the Commissioners consider reasonable. Fork F24: the last day of that year counts as before
-- its end. (b): for regulation 35, received after the end of the year in which the week falls, with no upper bound.
-- src:513 | An application must be received—
-- src:514 | (a) where the application is under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37—
-- src:515 | (i) before the end of the year following that in which a week, which is the subject of the application, falls, or
-- src:516 | (ii) within such further time as the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs, as the case may be, consider reasonable in the circumstances, or
-- src:517 | (b) where the application is under regulation 35, after the end of the year in which a week, which is the subject of the application, falls.
@ref Regulation 39 (src:513-517)
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of application under regulation 39`
      `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
      `the application` IS AN `An application for a credit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application is received in time` `the kind` `for the week beginning` `the first day of the week` `and the application being` `the application` MEANS
    IF   `the kind` EQUALS `an application under regulation 35`
    THEN Day (`the application`'s `the date the application is received`) GREATER THAN Day `the last day of the year the week falls in`
    ELSE     Day (`the application`'s `the date the application is received`) AT MOST Day `the last day of the year following`
          OR `the application`'s `the person who decides considers it reasonable to allow further time in the circumstances`
    WHERE
        `the year the week falls in` MEANS `the tax year a week falls in` `the first day of the week`
        `the last day of the year the week falls in` MEANS Date 5 4 (`the year the week falls in` PLUS 1)
        `the last day of the year following` MEANS Date 5 4 (`the year the week falls in` PLUS 2)

§§ `Regulation 29: credits under the 1975 Regulations`

-- src:355 | (1) Where a person is credited with earnings or contributions under the provisions of the 1975 Regulations specified in paragraph (2), the person is also to be credited with those earnings or contributions for the purposes of Part 1 of the 2014 Act.
-- src:356 | (2) The provisions specified are—
-- src:357 | (a) regulation 7 (credits for approved training);
-- src:358 | (b) regulation 7A (credits for carer’s allowance or carer support payment);
-- src:359 | (c) regulation 7B (credits for disability element of working tax credit);
-- src:360 | (d) regulation 8A (credits for unemployment);
-- src:361 | (e) regulation 8B (credits for incapacity for work or limited capability for work);
-- src:362 | (f) regulation 9B (credits for jury service);
-- src:363 | (g) regulation 9C (credits for maternity pay etc.);
-- src:364 | (h) regulation 9D (credits for certain periods of imprisonment or detention in legal custody);
-- src:365 | (i) regulation 9E (credits for certain spouses and civil partners of members of Her Majesty’s forces).
@ref Regulation 29(1), 29(2) (src:355-365)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision of the 1975 Regulations`
      `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `the provision` `for the week beginning` `the first day of the week` MEANS
        NOT (`the provision` EQUALS `some other provision of the 1975 Regulations`)
    AND `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` `the first day of the week`

§§ `Regulation 30: working tax credit`

-- Paragraph (2): where tax credit is paid in respect of a couple, "the person in respect of whom working tax credit is paid" is the
-- one member assessed as having earnings, or, where both members' earnings are assessed, the member to whom it is paid. Where it
-- is not paid in respect of a couple, it is the person it is paid to.
-- src:372 | (2) Where working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple, the reference in paragraph (1) to the person in respect of whom working tax credit is paid is a reference to —
-- src:373 | (a) where only one member of the couple is assessed for the purposes of the award of working tax credit as having income consisting of earnings, that member, or
-- src:374 | (b) where the earnings of each member are assessed, the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid.
@ref Regulation 30(2) (src:372-374)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit while working tax credit is paid`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is the person in respect of whom working tax credit is paid` `the facts` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`the facts`'s `the working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple`)
    THEN `the facts`'s `the working tax credit is paid to the person`
    ELSE IF   `the facts`'s `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings`
         THEN `the facts`'s `the person is the member assessed as having income consisting of earnings`
         ELSE     `the facts`'s `the earnings of each member of the couple are assessed`
              AND `the facts`'s `the working tax credit is paid to the person`

-- src:367 | (1) Where working tax credit is paid to a person in respect of a week in which the person is—
-- src:368 | (a) an employed earner,
-- src:369 | (b) a self-employed earner whose profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act, who would otherwise... be treated as having actually paid, a Class 2 contribution, or
-- src:370 | (c) excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001,
-- src:371 | the person is to be credited with earnings equal to the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of that week.
-- src:375 | (3) Paragraph (1) does not apply to—
-- src:376 | (a) a person in respect of a week in which the person is entitled to be credited with earnings under—
-- src:377 | (i) regulation 7B (credits for disability element of working tax credit),
-- src:378 | (ii) regulation 8A (credits for unemployment), or
-- src:379 | (iii) regulation 8B (credits for incapacity for work or limited capability for work),
-- src:380 | of the 1975 Regulations; or
-- src:381 | (b) a woman in respect of a week in any part of which an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force.
@ref Regulation 30(1), 30(3) (src:367-371); regulation 30(3) (src:375-381)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit while working tax credit is paid`
      `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`earnings are credited under regulation 30` `the facts` `for the week beginning` `the first day of the week` MEANS
        `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` `the first day of the week`
    AND `the facts`'s `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week`
    AND `the person is the person in respect of whom working tax credit is paid` `the facts`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `the person is an employed earner in the week`
         OR  `the facts`'s `the person is a self-employed earner whose profits for the year are below the small profits threshold, who would otherwise be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution`
         OR  `the facts`'s `the person is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001`)
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations`)
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week`)

-- "credited with earnings equal to the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of that week".
@ref Regulation 30(1) (src:371)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit while working tax credit is paid`
      `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earnings credited under regulation 30` `the facts` `for the week beginning` `the first day of the week` MEANS
    IF   `earnings are credited under regulation 30` `the facts` `for the week beginning` `the first day of the week`
    THEN `the facts`'s `the lower earnings limit in force for the week`
    ELSE 0

§§ `Regulation 31: universal credit`

-- src:384 | A person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of a week for any part of which the person is entitled to universal credit under Part 1 of the 2012 Act.
@ref Regulation 31 (src:384)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
      `the person is entitled to universal credit under Part 1 of the 2012 Act for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 31` `the first day of the week` `given` `the person is entitled to universal credit under Part 1 of the 2012 Act for any part of the week` MEANS
        `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` `the first day of the week`
    AND `the person is entitled to universal credit under Part 1 of the 2012 Act for any part of the week`

§§ `Regulation 32: men approaching pensionable age`

-- (2)(a): the year in which the man attains the age that is pensionable age for a woman born on the same day; (b) a subsequent year
-- before the one in which he attains 65. (3): not a year in which he is absent from Great Britain for more than 182 days. (4): a
-- self-employed man only if the Class 2 condition holds.
-- src:386 | (1) Subject to paragraph (4), a man born before 6th October 1953 is to be credited with earnings equal to the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of a week to which paragraph (2) applies.
-- src:387 | (2) This paragraph applies to a week which falls within—
-- src:388 | (a) the year in which the man attains the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day, and
-- src:389 | (b) a subsequent year prior to that in which he attains the age of 65.
-- src:390 | (3) Paragraph (2) does not apply to a week which falls within a year during which the man is absent from Great Britain for more than 182 days.
-- src:391 | (4) Paragraph (1) applies to a man who is a self-employed earner only if he—
-- src:392 | (a) ... would be treated as having actually paid, a Class 2 contribution but for the fact that his profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act, or
-- src:393 | (b) is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001 in respect of any week in a year to which this regulation applies.
@ref Regulation 32 (src:386-393)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for a man approaching pensionable age`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`earnings are credited under regulation 32` `the facts` MEANS
        `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`)
    AND `the facts`'s `the person is a man`
    AND Day (`the facts`'s `the man's date of birth`) LESS THAN Day (Date 6 10 1953)
    AND `the year of the week` AT LEAST `the year he attains the pensionable age of a woman born on the same day`
    AND `the year of the week` LESS THAN `the year he attains 65`
    AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `the number of days in the year of the week that the man was absent from Great Britain` GREATER THAN 182))
    AND (    (NOT `the facts`'s `the man is a self-employed earner`)
         OR  `the facts`'s `the man would be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution but for profits below the small profits threshold`
         OR  `the facts`'s `the man is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001`)
    WHERE
        `the year of the week` MEANS `the tax year a week falls in` (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`)
        `the year he attains the pensionable age of a woman born on the same day` MEANS `the tax year a calendar day falls in` (`the facts`'s `the date the man attains the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day`)
        `the year he attains 65` MEANS `the tax year a calendar day falls in` (`add years` (`the facts`'s `the man's date of birth`) 65)

@ref Regulation 32(1) (src:386)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for a man approaching pensionable age`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earnings credited under regulation 32` `the facts` MEANS
    IF   `earnings are credited under regulation 32` `the facts`
    THEN `the facts`'s `the lower earnings limit in force for the week`
    ELSE 0

§§ `Regulation 33: forces spouses, from 6 April 2016`

-- Paragraphs (2), (4), (5), (6) are those of regulation 28, and are the one rule `the conditions for a forces spouse's credit are met`.
-- src:395 | (1) Subject to paragraph (5), a person who satisfies the conditions in paragraph (2) for any part of a week to which this regulation applies is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of that week.
-- src:399 | (3) This regulation applies to a week which falls within a year beginning on or after 6th April 2016 for which the earnings factors of the member of Her Majesty’s forces exceed the qualifying earnings factor.
@ref Regulation 33(1), 33(3) (src:395); regulation 33(3) (src:399)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` `the facts` MEANS
        `the tax year a week falls in` (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`) AT LEAST DATE_YEAR `the date the Regulations come into force`
    AND `the facts`'s `the earnings factors of the member for the year of the week exceed the qualifying earnings factor`
    AND `the conditions for a forces spouse's credit are met` `the facts`

§§ `Regulation 34: child benefit`

-- src:413 | (1) A person is entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of a week in which the person is—
-- src:414 | (a) awarded child benefit for any part of that week in respect of a child under the age of 12, or
-- src:415 | (b) in the circumstances specified by paragraph (2) and subject to paragraph (3), the partner of a person to whom child benefit is awarded.
-- src:416 | (2) The circumstances are that the partner—
-- src:417 | (a) resides with the person to whom child benefit is awarded,
-- src:418 | (b) shares responsibility for the child in respect of whom child benefit is awarded with that person,
-- src:419 | (c) is ordinarily resident in Great Britain,
-- src:420 | (d) is not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody, and
-- src:421 | (e) makes an application to the Commissioners for Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs to be so credited in accordance with regulation 39.
-- src:422 | (3) Paragraph (1)(b) only applies in respect of a week that falls within a year for which the earnings factors of the person to whom child benefit is awarded exceed the qualifying earnings factor.
-- src:423 | (4) In calculating the earnings factors for the purpose of paragraph (3), no account is to be taken of any earnings factors derived from contributions credited by virtue of that person being awarded child benefit.
@ref Regulation 34 (src:413-423)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit in respect of child benefit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` `the facts` MEANS
        `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`)
    AND (    `the facts`'s `child benefit is awarded to the person for any part of the week in respect of a child under the age of 12`
         OR  `the partner is credited`)
    WHERE
        `the partner is credited` MEANS
                `the facts`'s `the person is the partner of a person to whom child benefit is awarded for the week`
            AND `the facts`'s `the partner resides with the person to whom child benefit is awarded`
            AND `the facts`'s `the partner shares responsibility for the child with that person`
            AND `the facts`'s `the partner is ordinarily resident in Great Britain`
            AND `the facts`'s `the partner is not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody`
            AND `the application is in time`
            AND `the facts`'s `the earnings factors of the person to whom child benefit is awarded for the year exceed the qualifying earnings factor`
        `the application is in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the partner has applied to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST `an application` THEN `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b)` `for the week beginning` (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`) `and the application being` `an application`

§§ `Regulation 35: care for a child under 12`

-- Paragraph (6)(a) to (k): the persons who may be credited; the relationship is a stated input.
-- src:443 | (6) The person specified in paragraph (2)(b) is—
-- src:444 | (a) a non-resident parent;
-- src:445 | (b) a grandparent;
-- src:446 | (c) a great-grandparent;
-- src:447 | (d) a great-great-grandparent;
-- src:448 | (e) a sibling;
-- src:449 | (f) a parent’s sibling;
-- src:450 | (g) a spouse or former spouse of any persons listed in sub-paragraphs (a) to (f);
-- src:451 | (h) a civil partner or former civil partner of any persons listed in sub-paragraphs (a) to (f);
-- src:452 | (i) a partner or former partner of any persons listed in sub-paragraphs (a) to (h);
-- src:453 | (j) a son or daughter of any persons listed in sub-paragraphs (e) to (i);
-- src:454 | (k) in respect of a son or daughter of a person listed in sub-paragraph (f), that person’s—
-- src:455 | (i) spouse or former spouse,
-- src:456 | (ii) civil partner or former civil partner, or
-- src:457 | (iii) partner or former partner.
@ref Regulation 35(6) (src:443-457)
GIVEN `the relationship` IS A `Relationship to the child cared for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the relationship is one regulation 35(6) specifies` `the relationship` MEANS
    NOT (`the relationship` EQUALS `none of the relationships in regulation 35(6)`)

-- Paragraph (7): for (6)(e) and (f), a sibling includes a sibling of the half blood, a step sibling and an adopted sibling.
-- src:458 | (7) For the purposes of paragraph (6)(e) and (f), a sibling includes a sibling of the half blood, a step sibling and an adopted sibling.
@ref Regulation 35(7) (src:458)
GIVEN `of the whole blood` IS A BOOLEAN
      `of the half blood` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a step sibling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adopted sibling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person counts as a sibling under regulation 35(7)` `of the whole blood` `or` `of the half blood` `or` `a step sibling` `or` `an adopted sibling` MEANS
    `of the whole blood` OR `of the half blood` OR `a step sibling` OR `an adopted sibling`

-- Paragraph (8): for (6)(i) and (k)(iii), a partner is the other member of a couple who are not married to, or civil partners of, each
-- other but are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
-- src:459 | (8) For the purposes of paragraph (6)(i) and (k)(iii), a partner is a person who is the other member of a couple who are not married to, or civil partners of, each other but are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
@ref Regulation 35(8) (src:459)
GIVEN `the person is the other member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are married to, or civil partners of, each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they live together as if they were a married couple or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person counts as a partner under regulation 35(8)` `the person is the other member of a couple` `and` `they are married to, or civil partners of, each other` `and` `they live together as if they were a married couple or civil partners` MEANS
        `the person is the other member of a couple`
    AND (NOT `they are married to, or civil partners of, each other`)
    AND `they live together as if they were a married couple or civil partners`

-- Paragraph (5): what the application must include.
-- src:439 | (5) An application under paragraph (3)(c) must—
-- src:440 | (a) include the name and date of birth of the child , or each child, cared for,
-- src:441 | (b) where requested by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs, include a declaration by B that the conditions in paragraph (2) are satisfied, and
-- src:442 | (c) specify the relevant week or weeks in which the child , or each child, was cared for.
@ref Regulation 35(5) (src:439-442)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit for caring for a child under 12`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application meets regulation 35(5)` `the facts` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `the application includes the name and date of birth of each child cared for`
    AND (    (NOT `the facts`'s `the Secretary of State or the Commissioners requested a declaration by the other person`)
         OR  `the facts`'s `the application includes a declaration by the other person that the conditions in regulation 35(2) are satisfied`)
    AND `the facts`'s `the application specifies the week or weeks in which each child was cared for`

-- Paragraph (4): where more than one person could be credited for the week, they elect, with the agreement of the person awarded child
-- benefit, which of them is credited (and only that one); in default of agreement, it is for the Secretary of State to decide.
-- src:436 | (4) Where the requirements relating to the provision of care by A in paragraph (3)(a)(i) can be satisfied by more than one person in respect of a week in which B was awarded child benefit—
-- src:437 | (a) those persons shall elect, with the agreement of B, which of them is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution credit (and then only the elected person is to be so credited), or
-- src:438 | (b) the Secretary of State is to exercise his discretion to determine which of those persons is to be credited with that contribution, in default of the agreement referred to in sub-paragraph (a).
@ref Regulation 35(4) (src:436-438)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit for caring for a child under 12`
GIVETH A `Whether a credit is given`
`who is credited where more than one person could be` `the facts` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`the facts`'s `more than one person could be credited for the week`)
    THEN `the credit is given`
    ELSE IF   `the facts`'s `those persons have elected, with the agreement of the other person, which of them is to be credited`
         THEN IF   `the facts`'s `this person is the one elected`
              THEN `the credit is given`
              ELSE `the credit is not given`
         ELSE `the credit is left to the Secretary of State's discretion`

-- src:425 | (1) Subject to paragraphs (3) and (4), a person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of a week (“the relevant week”) in which the conditions in paragraph (2) are satisfied.
-- src:426 | (2) The conditions are that in the relevant week the person—
-- src:427 | (a) provided care in respect of a child under the age of 12,
-- src:428 | (b) is, in relation to that child, a person specified in paragraph (6), and
-- src:429 | (c) was ordinarily resident in Great Britain.
-- src:430 | (3) The person (‘A’) referred to in paragraph (1) is not entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution unless—
-- src:431 | (a) child benefit was awarded to another person (‘B’) in respect of—
-- src:432 | (i) the child, or each child, for whom A provided care, and
-- src:433 | (ii) the week in which A provided that care,
-- src:434 | (b) B’s earnings factors, other than those derived from a Class 3 contribution credit awarded under regulation 34, exceed the qualifying earnings factor for the year in which the relevant week falls, and
-- src:435 | (c) A makes an application to the Secretary of State to be so credited in accordance with paragraph (5) and regulation 39.
@ref Regulation 35(1), 35(2), 35(3) (src:425-435)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit for caring for a child under 12`
      `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Whether a credit is given`
`whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` `the facts` `for the week beginning` `the first day of the week` MEANS
    IF   `the conditions of paragraphs (2) and (3) are met`
    THEN `who is credited where more than one person could be` `the facts`
    ELSE `the credit is not given`
    WHERE
        `the conditions of paragraphs (2) and (3) are met` MEANS
                `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` `the first day of the week`
            AND `the facts`'s `the person provided care in the week in respect of a child under the age of 12`
            AND `the relationship is one regulation 35(6) specifies` (`the facts`'s `the person's relationship to the child`)
            AND `the facts`'s `the person was ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week`
            AND `the facts`'s `child benefit was awarded to another person in respect of the child, or each child, and the week`
            AND `the facts`'s `that other person's earnings factors, other than those derived from a regulation 34 credit, exceed the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
            AND `the application is made in order and in time`
        `the application is made in order and in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the person has applied to the Secretary of State`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST `an application` THEN
                    `the application meets regulation 35(5)` `the facts`
                AND `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 35` `for the week beginning` `the first day of the week` `and the application being` `an application`

§§ `Regulation 36: foster parents`

-- src:461 | (1) Subject to paragraph (3), a person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of a week in which the person is a foster parent and is—
-- src:462 | (a) ordinarily resident in Great Britain, and
-- src:463 | (b) not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody.
-- src:464 | (2) For the purposes of this regulation, a foster parent is a person approved as—
-- src:465 | (a) a foster parent in accordance with Part 5 (approval of foster parents) of the Fostering Services (England) Regulations 2011,
-- src:466 | (b) a kinship carer in accordance with Part 5 (kinship care) of the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009,
-- src:467 | (c) a foster carer in accordance with Part 7 (fostering) of those Regulations, or
-- src:468 | (d) a foster parent in accordance with Part 2 (approvals and placements) of the Foster Placement (Children) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1996.
-- src:469 | (3) A person is not entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution under paragraph (1) unless an application to be so credited is received by the Commissioners for Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs in accordance with regulation 39.
@ref Regulation 36 (src:461-469)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit as a foster parent`
      `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` `the facts` `for the week beginning` `the first day of the week` MEANS
        `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` `the first day of the week`
    AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `the person's approval` EQUALS `not approved under any of those provisions`))
    AND `the facts`'s `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain`
    AND `the facts`'s `the person is not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody`
    AND `the application is in time`
    WHERE
        `the application is in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the person has applied to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST `an application` THEN `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 36` `for the week beginning` `the first day of the week` `and the application being` `an application`

§§ `Regulation 37: caring`

-- Paragraph (7): an appropriate person is involved in the person cared for's health care or social care and is considered by the
-- Secretary of State as appropriate to make a declaration as to the level of care required.
-- src:502 | (7) For the purposes of paragraph (6)(d), an appropriate person is a person who is—
-- src:503 | (a) involved in the health care or social care of the person cared for, and
-- src:504 | (b) considered by the Secretary of State as appropriate to make a declaration as to the level of care required.
@ref Regulation 37(7) (src:502-504)
GIVEN `the person is involved in the health care or social care of the person cared for` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State considers the person appropriate to make a declaration as to the level of care required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is an appropriate person` `the person is involved in the health care or social care of the person cared for` `and` `the Secretary of State considers the person appropriate to make a declaration as to the level of care required` MEANS
        `the person is involved in the health care or social care of the person cared for`
    AND `the Secretary of State considers the person appropriate to make a declaration as to the level of care required`

-- Paragraph (4): a relevant benefit is one of those listed.
-- src:480 | (4) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(a)(i), “relevant benefit” means—
-- src:481 | (a) attendance allowance in accordance with section 64 of the 1992 Act;
-- src:482 | (aa) pension age disability payment in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024;
-- src:483 | (b) the care component of disability living allowance in accordance with section 72 of the 1992 Act, at the middle or highest rate prescribed in accordance with subsection (3) of that section;
-- src:484 | (c) an increase in the rate of disablement pension in accordance with section 104 of the 1992 Act;
-- src:485 | (d) any benefit which is payable as if an injury or disease were one in respect of which a disablement pension would for the time being be payable in respect of an assessment of 100 per cent., by virtue of—
-- src:486 | (i) the Pneumoconiosis, Byssinosis and Miscellaneous Diseases Benefit Scheme 1983; or
-- src:487 | (ii) regulations made under section 64(3) of the 2012 Act (injuries arising before 5 July 1948);
-- src:488 | (e) a constant attendance allowance payable by virtue of—
-- src:489 | (i) article 8 (constant attendance allowance) of the Naval, Military and Air Forces etc. (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 2006; or
-- src:490 | (ii) article 14 (constant attendance allowance) of the Personal Injuries (Civilians) Scheme 1983;
-- src:491 | (f) the daily living component of personal independence payment in accordance with section 78 of the 2012 Act;
-- src:492 | (g) armed forces independence payment in accordance with the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011.
-- src:493 | (h) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11 of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021;
-- src:494 | (i) the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate payable in accordance with regulation 5 of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022;
-- src:495 | (j) the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025.
@ref Regulation 37(4) (src:480-495)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A `Relevant benefit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the benefit is a relevant benefit` `the benefit` MEANS
    NOT (`the benefit` EQUALS `none of those benefits`)

-- Paragraph (2): engaged in caring if (a) caring for 20 or more hours in the week and every person cared for is entitled to a relevant
-- benefit, or the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate; or (b) paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income
-- Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies. Paragraph (3): not during any period of not being ordinarily resident in Great Britain
-- or of imprisonment or detention in legal custody.
-- src:472 | (2) A person is engaged in caring in a week if the person is—
-- src:473 | (a) caring for another person or persons for a total of 20 or more hours in that week and—
-- src:474 | (i) that other person is, or each of the persons cared for are, entitled to a relevant benefit for that week, or
-- src:475 | (ii) the Secretary of State considers that level of care to be appropriate; or
-- src:476 | (b) a person to whom one or more of paragraphs 4 to 6 (persons caring for another person) of Schedule 1B (prescribed categories of person) to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies.
-- src:477 | (3) A person is not engaged in caring for the purposes of this regulation during any period in respect of which the person is—
-- src:478 | (a) not ordinarily resident in Great Britain, or
-- src:479 | (b) undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody.
@ref Regulation 37(2), 37(3) (src:472-479)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit for caring`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is engaged in caring under paragraph (2)(a)` `the facts` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `the hours the person cared for another person or persons in the week` AT LEAST 20
    AND (    (    count (`the facts`'s `the benefit each person cared for is entitled to for the week`) AT LEAST 1
              AND all (GIVEN `a benefit` YIELD `the benefit is a relevant benefit` `a benefit`) (`the facts`'s `the benefit each person cared for is entitled to for the week`))
         OR  `the facts`'s `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate`)

@ref Regulation 37(2), 37(3) (src:472-479)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit for caring`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is not excluded from caring by paragraph (3)` `the facts` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week`
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody in the week`)

-- Paragraph (6): what the application must include.
-- src:497 | (6) An application under paragraph (5) must include—
-- src:498 | (a) a declaration by the applicant that the applicant cares for a person or persons for 20 or more hours in a week,
-- src:499 | (b) the name and, where known, the national insurance number of each person cared for,
-- src:500 | (c) where applicable, which relevant benefit each person cared for is entitled to, and
-- src:501 | (d) where requested by the Secretary of State, a declaration signed by an appropriate person as to the level of care which is required for each person cared for.
@ref Regulation 37(6) (src:497-501)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit for caring`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application meets regulation 37(6)` `the facts` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `the application includes a declaration by the applicant that the applicant cares for 20 or more hours in a week`
    AND `the facts`'s `the application includes the name and, where known, the national insurance number of each person cared for`
    AND `the facts`'s `the application says, where applicable, which relevant benefit each person cared for is entitled to`
    AND (    (NOT `the facts`'s `the Secretary of State requested a declaration by an appropriate person as to the level of care`)
         OR  `the facts`'s `the application includes a declaration signed by an appropriate person as to the level of care`)

-- Paragraph (1): a Class 3 contribution for a week in which the person is engaged in caring. Paragraph (5): a credit under (2)(a)
-- needs an application (paragraph (6) and regulation 39), "except in a case to which paragraph (8) applies": a woman with an election
-- in force. Read literally, paragraph (8) removes the need for an application from her, not her credit (fork F25); a credit under
-- (2)(b) never needs one.
-- src:471 | (1) Subject to paragraph (5), a person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of a week in which the person is engaged in caring.
-- src:496 | (5) Except in a case to which paragraph (8) applies, a person is not entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution under paragraph (2)(a) unless an application to be so credited is received by the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (6) and regulation 39.
-- src:505 | (8) This paragraph applies in the case of a woman in respect of a week in any part of which an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force.
@ref Regulation 37(1), 37(5), 37(8) (src:471); regulation 37(5) (src:496); regulation 37(8) (src:505)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit for caring`
      `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` `the facts` `for the week beginning` `the first day of the week` MEANS
        `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` `the first day of the week`
    AND `the person is not excluded from caring by paragraph (3)` `the facts`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to the person`
         OR  (    `the person is engaged in caring under paragraph (2)(a)` `the facts`
              AND (    `the facts`'s `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week`
                   OR  `the application is in order and in time`)))
    WHERE
        `the application is in order and in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the person has applied to the Secretary of State`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST `an application` THEN
                    `the application meets regulation 37(6)` `the facts`
                AND `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 37` `for the week beginning` `the first day of the week` `and the application being` `an application`

§§ `Regulation 38: an additional period`

-- Twelve weeks (84 days): (1)(a) before the day entitlement begins; (1)(b) after the week in which entitlement to carer's allowance
-- or carer support payment ends, but not in a week of entitlement under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations (paragraph (2));
-- (1)(c) after a week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied. A week is counted by its first day: for (a) it lies in the 84
-- days ending the day before the day entitlement begins (so there are twelve such weeks); for (b) and (c) it is one of the twelve
-- weeks after the week in which entitlement or the satisfaction ends (fork F26).
-- src:507 | (1) A person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution for a period of 12 weeks—
-- src:508 | (a) prior to the date on which that person becomes entitled to carer’s allowance by virtue of subsection (1) of section 70 of the 1992 Act or the carer support payment component of carer support given in accordance with the Carer’s Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023;
-- src:509 | (b) subject to paragraph (2), following the end of the week in which that person ceases to be entitled to carer’s allowance by virtue of that subsection or the carer support payment component of carer support by virtue of those Regulations;
-- src:510 | (c) following the end of a week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied.
-- src:511 | (2) A person is not entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution under paragraph (1)(b) in a week in respect of which that person is entitled under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations to be credited with contributions by virtue of being entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the 1992 Act or the carer support payment component of carer support given in accordance with the Carer’s Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023.
@ref Regulation 38 (src:507-511)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for an additional period of credit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` `the facts` MEANS
        `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`)
    AND CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the circumstance`
        WHEN `before becoming entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` THEN
                Day (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`) AT LEAST (Day (`the facts`'s `the day entitlement begins, or the first day of the week in which it ends`) MINUS 84)
            AND Day (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`) LESS THAN Day (`the facts`'s `the day entitlement begins, or the first day of the week in which it ends`)
        WHEN `after ceasing to be entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` THEN
                Day (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`) AT LEAST (Day (`the facts`'s `the day entitlement begins, or the first day of the week in which it ends`) PLUS 7)
            AND Day (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`) AT MOST (Day (`the facts`'s `the day entitlement begins, or the first day of the week in which it ends`) PLUS 84)
            AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the person is entitled in the week under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations to be credited because of carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support`)
        WHEN `after a week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied` THEN
                Day (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`) AT LEAST (Day (`the facts`'s `the day entitlement begins, or the first day of the week in which it ends`) PLUS 7)
            AND Day (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`) AT MOST (Day (`the facts`'s `the day entitlement begins, or the first day of the week in which it ends`) PLUS 84)
